  nonce: 18a2  # 18a2
  message: "CLOSED ON THE FILED INSTANCE. The residual is filed as WI-fihun.\n\nWHAT LANDED. `method-call-recovery-linker` now refuses outright when the unresolved edge it is resolving carries a COMPLETE external identity key — `dst_ref` with a module path, ADR-0035's key, stated positively or abstained per ADR-0057 §15.1. The producer that read the imports and the scope made a claim about WHERE the callee lives; this linker has a short name, a class hint and a line-proximity tiebreaker, which is strictly less evidence, so an in-repo answer CONTRADICTS the claim rather than filling a gap. §11 settles that contest by keeping both edges and §14 (as of PR #1100) declines to demote; this applies the same rule one stage earlier, at the pass that would otherwise manufacture the contest. `ir.stated_module_of` is the one reader of the partial/complete distinction, shared with §14 and §15's fold.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL EVIDENCE, re-running this row's own repro. `hypergumbo survey . --out survey.json` on this repository, single-backend Python:\n  - method-call-recovery edges: **92 -> 64**, 28 removed\n  - all 28 removed are in the hand-audited wrong set; 26 of them targeted a dataclass FIELD\n    (tree_sitter_rust.language -> Symbol.language x19, builtins.id -> Symbol.id,\n     builtins.type -> IpcPattern.type / PhoenixPattern.type / FieldSchema.type,\n     tree_sitter_lua.language -> Symbol.language), 2 targeted a method\n    (os.environ.get -> TrackerSet.get, pathlib.Path.exists -> TrackerSet.exists)\n  - `inherited-calls-linker` unchanged at 329 edges; §14 demotions stay 0\n  - precision on this corpus: **51% -> 73%** (45 wrong of 92 -> 17 wrong of 64)\nArtifacts: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/adr0057_q4_after/survey.json (before), rulik_after/survey.json (after).\n\nTHE REFUSAL IS PER CALL, NOT PER SITE. It reads the unresolved edge the recovery was derived FROM. `a.b(c.d())` puts two calls on one line and one sibling's module claim says nothing about the other — a site-keyed version of this gate would have refused 7 recoveries whose own stub abstained. Pinned by `test_the_refusal_is_per_call_not_per_site`.\n\nWHAT IS NOT ASSERTED. This row's title says the linker binds at ~49% precision. That number is falsified — it is 73% — but the linker is NOT correct: **17 of the remaining 64 edges are still wrong**, every one a receiver-blind mis-bind where the stub abstained, no `receiver_type_hint` was stamped (0 of 90 audited Python stubs carried one), and line proximity chose a same-named method on an unrelated class. Two more bind a `calls` edge to an `int`-declared field. Those are WI-fihun, which also carries the callability-taxonomy question and the two disagreeing hardcoded `_CALLABLE_KINDS` sets (`ranking.py:919` vs `entrypoints.py:1323`). I am closing this row rather than re-scoping it because the instance it was filed on — 28 edges overriding a correct external stub — is measurably gone; if the owner reads the title as covering the whole precision problem, reopen and I will fold WI-fihun back in.\n\nPR: #<filled on merge>."  # 18a2
